1. Manage Password Policy of user:
   Command: chage  ---> ch: change  ,  Age: Aging (time frame) 

   Managing user:
   a) Existing users    
      To manage passwd policy use "chage" command 
      ==> Set Account Expiry for the user bob after 45 days. 
      # chage -l <user_name>
      # man chage | grep 180
        chage -E $(date -d +180days +%Y-%m-%d)

      # chage -E $(date -d +45days +%Y-%m-%d) <user_name>
      # chage -l <user_name>     
     
     ==> Set Account Expiry for the user bob after 60 days and ensure password change on the next login. 
      
      # chage -l <user_name>
      # man chage | grep 180
        chage -E $(date -d +180days +%Y-%m-%d)

      # chage -d 0 -E $(date -d +60days +%Y-%m-%d) <user_name>
      # chage -l <user_name>     


   b) New Users
      # vim /etc/login.defs
  
      In esc mode /PASS_MAX
      PASS_MAX_EXPIRY  90

     # useradd <user_name>
     # chage -l <user_name>
